Now I understand the issue. `build_where` calls `_add_q` with `simple_col=True`. In `_add_q`, `simple_col` is only passed to `build_filter` for leaf children (the `else` branch). But when a child is a `Node` (i.e., a nested Q object), the recursive call to `_add_q` does NOT pass `simple_col`:

```python
if isinstance(child, Node):
    child_clause, needed_inner = self._add_q(
        child, used_aliases, branch_negated,
        current_negated, allow_joins, split_subq)
    joinpromoter.add_votes(needed_inner)
else:
    child_clause, needed_inner = self.build_filter(
        child, can_reuse=used_aliases, branch_negated=branch_negated,
        current_negated=current_negated, allow_joins=allow_joins,
        split_subq=split_subq, simple_col=simple_col,
    )
```

So the fix is to pass `simple_col=simple_col` to the recursive `_add_q` call. That way nested Q objects also use SimpleCol.

