Now I understand `set_values`. The bug: `get_combinator_sql` only calls `set_values` on combined queries when `not compiler.query.values_select`. But since the combined query objects are shared (qs1.union(qs1) uses the same query object twice, and the query object is mutated), after the first evaluation, `values_select` is already set, so subsequent evaluations with different columns don't update it.

