1. `hasattr(obj.model, item)` is used to detect whether the item is an attribute of the model. But `hasattr` may return False if accessing the attribute raises an exception other than `AttributeError` (or if the descriptor's `__get__` raises an exception on the class). In the case of PositionField, the `get` method throws an exception when accessed on the model class rather than an instance.

2. When `hasattr(obj.model, item)` is False, the code immediately returns E108 without trying `obj.model._meta.get_field(item)`.

