The issue is in `CheckboxInput.get_context()`. It modifies the passed-in `attrs` dict directly by setting `attrs['checked'] = True`. When `SplitArrayField` renders multiple widgets, they all share the same `attrs` dict, so after the first True value, `checked` stays in the dict for subsequent widgets.

The fix is to not mutate the passed-in attrs. Instead, create a copy or use the returned attrs from `super().get_context()`.

Let me look at how other widgets handle this. Let me look at the PR reference (https://github.com/django/django/pull/12193) hint. The typical fix:

```python
def get_context(self, name, value, attrs):
    if self.check_test(value):
        if attrs is None:
            attrs = {}
        attrs['checked'] = True
    return super().get_context(name, value, attrs)
```

