THOUGHT: Bug confirmed. The issue is at line 264 in parse_bits: it checks `param not in unhandled_kwargs` instead of checking all keyword-only parameters (`kwonly`). Since `unhandled_kwargs` excludes kwonly args with defaults, passing such an arg is treated as unexpected. Also, once a kwonly arg is consumed, it's removed from `unhandled_kwargs`, so a duplicate triggers the "unexpected" error instead of "multiple values". Let me check existing tests before making the fix

