Now, let me understand the issue more. The problem is in `generate_created_models`. When creating Book, Book inherits from Readable which has `title` in the old state. The autodetector will:
1. generate_deleted_models - but Readable is NOT deleted, so nothing happens for it
2. generate_created_models - Book is created with `title` field, depends on Readable being created (it exists already so no dependency issue)
3. generate_removed_fields - later removes `title` from Readable

So the CreateModel for Book happens before RemoveField for Readable.title. When migrating, CreateModel for Book tries to create a `title` field on Book which clashes with the inherited `title` from Readable (which still exists at that point).

The fix: In `generate_created_models`, for each field in the new model that exists in the from-state base models (i.e., the field is being removed from the base and added to the subclass), add a dependency `(base_app_label, base_model_name, field_name, False)` to the CreateModel operation. This will make the RemoveField operation run before the CreateModel.

