I need to be careful with flock semantics: `flock` locks are associated with an open file description. Two separate `open()` calls create two different open file descriptions, so a second non-blocking exclusive lock on a new fd while the first holds it should fail. On most platforms, flock works with open file descriptions, so this test should work.

