The issue: `__instancecheck__` uses `isinstance(instance, self._subclasses)` which correctly checks subclasses of BigAutoField/SmallAutoField. But `__subclasscheck__` uses `subclass in self._subclasses` which only checks exact classes in the tuple, not subclasses of those classes. So a subclass of BigAutoField fails `issubclass(MyBigAutoField, AutoField)`.

Fix: in `__subclasscheck__`, use `issubclass(subclass, self._subclasses) or super().__subclasscheck__(subclass)`.

