The issue described:
- Model formsets don't provide a way to create an "edit only" view of objects.
- Setting `extra=0` doesn't reliably prevent creating new objects because extra is just the number of extra forms displayed. You can add more forms with JavaScript (or just send additional post data).
- The user mentions the PR at https://github.com/django/django/pull/11580

So the fix is to add an `edit_only` parameter to `modelformset_factory` (and `BaseModelFormSet`) which, when True, disallows new object creation.

