Wait, but the issue says: "Moreover they don't call create(), get_or_create(), and update_or_create() respectively from a related manager but from the QuerySet."

So the async versions copied from QuerySet onto Manager call `self.get_queryset().acreate(...)`, which calls `QuerySet.create(...)`, NOT the related manager's `create`. So the FK constraint isn't set automatically. E.g., `author.book_set.acreate(title="X")` wouldn't set `author_id` on the created book.

So the fix is to add proper async methods to related managers that delegate to the related manager's own sync methods via `sync_to_async(self.create)`, etc.

