The `add_subparsers()` method of `ArgumentParser` accepts `parser_class` kwarg: "The class of this parser will be used to create subparser instances. By default, this is the class of the current parser (e.g. an ArgumentParser)."

So if we call `parser.add_subparsers(parser_class=type(parser))` it would use `CommandParser`. But then the subparsers created via `add_parser()` would be `CommandParser(**kwargs)`, without `missing_args_message` and `called_from_command_line`. Actually `add_parser()` passes kwargs to the parser class constructor. Let me check argparse source.

